{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"d2b69be861e0399ca189d66cc4119a5fab774b8fdcb5e98e45ada3ee0e73191d","digest":{"component_or_area":"grounding harness worker spawning","key_entities":["src/rebar/grounding/harness.py","run_in_worker","multiprocessing.get_context","Process.start","RunResult","multiprocessing/popen_fork.py","SpawnProcess","ForkProcess","tests/unit/grounding/test_spawn_contract.py"],"problem_keywords":["multiprocessing","fork","deadlock","spawn","serialization","worker","pickleable","thread-safety","multiprocessing context"],"propositions":["Hard-coded fork-based process spawning in POSIX hosts triggers CPython 3.12+ DeprecationWarning when run_in_worker executes under a live background thread, risking deadlock","Fork-context spawning permits unpickleable callables and closures that fail under spawn, hiding the serialization contract and creating incompatibility with Python 3.14 defaults","Spawn-based spawning requires callables to be importable module-level names and all arguments/return values to be pickleable, enforcing a forward-compatible portable contract","Process start, pickle, and receive/unpickle exceptions must map to fail-open RunResult(abstain_reason='other') rather than propagate to preserve the documented never-raise contract"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787476225334624001,"uuid":"0f2dd7c2-cae7-440b-9e8e-d6000a0f7eab"}